{
    "title": "Where is my car",
    "description": "This app helps find your car after you park it. Sometimes it is difficult to remember  where exactly the car parking was. This app tries to make this process automated and easy.\r\n\r\n\u2022 App saves car parking location automatically based on activity recognition algorithm provided by the Android OS. It detects the exact location, saves parking start time. Optionally it may notify you that parking was started but mainly it does everything automatically. Sometimes false positives may occur especially when you are underground. Also detection algorithm does not know if you are in your car or on public transport now. If false positives annoy you then it is always possible to completely switch off this feature in Settings. Or you may switch off just notifications.\r\n\r\n\u2022 The last parking location is clearly shown on the map. Both normal and satellite maps are supported. You may drag the car position marker to adjust the car location directly on map.\r\n\r\n\u2022 Another great view for the car parking is Radar view. It works even without Internet connection. It is best to find your car on parking. Radar clearly shows direction and distance to your car. It uses GPS, accelerometer and magnetometer of your phone to calculate the location where car is and direction for you to go.\r\n\r\n\u2022 App supports photo attachments. Sometimes, especially on underground parking the GPS is not quite accurate. And in these cases you may attach photo of your parking lot. Then you may easily find that parking lot among other cars.\r\n\r\n\u2022 Car parking time is counted and is shown clearly. Now you always know how long your car is on park and how much money your should pay if parking is not free.\r\n\r\n\u2022 All your parking sessions are saved in the app. So it is always possible to view history of your parking sessions.\r\n\r\n\u2022 App supports kilometers as well as miles for distance readings. This setting affects Radar view.",
    "descriptionHTML": "This app helps find your car after you park it. Sometimes it is difficult to remember  where exactly the car parking was. This app tries to make this process automated and easy.<br><br>\u2022 App saves car parking location automatically based on activity recognition algorithm provided by the Android OS. It detects the exact location, saves parking start time. Optionally it may notify you that parking was started but mainly it does everything automatically. Sometimes false positives may occur especially when you are underground. Also detection algorithm does not know if you are in your car or on public transport now. If false positives annoy you then it is always possible to completely switch off this feature in Settings. Or you may switch off just notifications.<br><br>\u2022 The last parking location is clearly shown on the map. Both normal and satellite maps are supported. You may drag the car position marker to adjust the car location directly on map.<br><br>\u2022 Another great view for the car parking is Radar view. It works even without Internet connection. It is best to find your car on parking. Radar clearly shows direction and distance to your car. It uses GPS, accelerometer and magnetometer of your phone to calculate the location where car is and direction for you to go.<br><br>\u2022 App supports photo attachments. Sometimes, especially on underground parking the GPS is not quite accurate. And in these cases you may attach photo of your parking lot. Then you may easily find that parking lot among other cars.<br><br>\u2022 Car parking time is counted and is shown clearly. Now you always know how long your car is on park and how much money your should pay if parking is not free.<br><br>\u2022 All your parking sessions are saved in the app. So it is always possible to view history of your parking sessions.<br><br>\u2022 App supports kilometers as well as miles for distance readings. This setting affects Radar view.",
